    FEAT-0001: use Facilities' field names in the bookings file
    
    Facilities' other tools read data/bookings.json too, and they call a
    booking's times startTime and endTime. The file now uses those names.
    
    No rule changed: the 2-hour limit and overlaps work exactly as before.
    But the overlap check had to change anyway, because the rules read the
    same objects that are stored in the file, so they use its field names.
    
    Two of the three tests broke. Every test hands FakeFileSystem a JSON
    string, or reads back the JSON that book() wrote, so the tests knew the
    file's field names too: the shared fixture and the expected JSON had to
    change. Only the 2-hour test passed, because it refuses the request
    before it ever looks at another booking.

